error: I64 has more than one method named `shout`
  --> methods.norn:49:15
   |
49 |     let d = 3.shout()
   |               ^^^^^ ambiguous method
   = note: `Loud` provides one
   = note: `Quiet` provides one
   = note: methods share one name and functions do not: call the function form the impl delegates to

error: `user` was given away
  --> methods.norn:65:22
   |
65 |     user.consume() + user.consume()
   |                      ^^^^ used here
  --> methods.norn:65:5
   |
65 |     user.consume() + user.consume()
   |     ^^^^ given here
   = note: a `User` copies, but it was handed to a `sink` parameter, and the name does not survive that
   = note: `let kept = user` before the call keeps a copy under a name of its own

